  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Key finding driving this list: `packages/react-scripts/config/webpack.config.js` in create-react-app v5.0.1 still contains a production-profiling webpack alias (`'scheduler/tracing': 'scheduler/tracing-profiling'`, alongside `'react-dom$': 'react-dom/profiling'`) targeting the `scheduler/tracing` module family. That module was removed from React starting at v17 (confirmed by `packages/react-devtools-shared/src/backend/renderer.js`'s comment \"The scheduler/tracing API was removed in v17 though\", and by `packages/scheduler/package.json`'s `files` list in React 18.2.0, which ships only `index.js`, `unstable_mock.js`, and `unstable_post_task.js` \u2014 no `tracing.js`/`tracing-profiling.js`). CRA's alias is dead/vestigial: it only fires when a user runs a production build with `--profile`, and would resolve to a nonexistent module in React 18. `react-dom/profiling` itself is still valid (confirmed via `packages/react-dom/package.json` exports), so only the scheduler-side half of that pairing is dead.\n\nSecondary evidence included: React's `__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED` export sites (`packages/react/src/React.js`, `packages/react-dom/src/client/ReactDOM.js`) for completeness, though CRA templates don't reference these directly; CRA's actual render entrypoint (`cra-template/.../index.js`) already uses `ReactDOM.createRoot`, ruling out the more obvious `ReactDOM.render` deprecation as a hit; and `setupTests.js`/`react-scripts/package.json` showing CRA's test stack uses `@testing-library/jest-dom` rather than the deprecated `react-dom/test-utils` surface directly.",
